  "worked_solution": "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2,3}=-1\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-4(x-5)(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =-4(x-5)(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4(x-5)(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -4(x-5)({x}^{2}-x(-1-2\\text{i})-x(-1+2\\text{i})+(-1+2\\text{i})(-1-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -4(x-5)({x}^{2}+2x+5) & = \\\\ -4({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+5x-5{x}^{2}-10x-25) & = \\\\ -4({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-5x-25) & = \\\\ -4{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+20x+100.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-4{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+20x+100.$",
